TI  - Integrating Embedded Multiagent Systems with Urban Simulation Tools and IoT Applications
FAU - Lucas Fernando Souza de Castro
FAU - Fabian César Pereira Brandão Manoel
FAU - Vinicius Souza de Jesus
FAU - Carlos Eduardo Pantoja
FAU - André Pinz Borges
FAU - Gleifer Vaz Alves
DP  - 2022
AID - 10.22456/2175-2745.110837 [doi]
AB  - The smart city systems development connected to the Internet of Things (IoT) has been the goal of several works in the multi-agent system field. Nevertheless, just a few projects demonstrate how to deploy and make the connection among the employed systems. This paper proposes an approach towards the integration of a MAS through the JaCaMo framework plus an Urban Simulation Tool (SUMO), IoT applications (Node-RED, InfluxDB, and Grafana), and an IoT platform (Konker). The integration presented in this paper applies in a Smart Parking scenario with real features, where is shown the integration and the connection through all layers, from agent level to artifacts, including real environment and simulation, as well as IoT applications. In future works, we intend to establish a methodology that shows how to properly integrate these different applications regardless of the scenario and the used tools.
