AB  - During the COVID-19 pandemic, the Federal University of Rio Grande do Norte (UFRN) adopted the emergency remote regime for its academic activities. In this scenario, the Multiprova software played a key role in facilitating the teaching-learning process at the institution. With the resumption of face-to-face classes, the need to improve the evaluation of tests arose. One of the solutions implemented was the automatic correction of answer cards filled in by hand by students. The main focus of this project is to optimize the proof correction procedure in the Multiprova software by applying handwritten character recognition techniques through convolutional neural networks. Answer-card images, obtained directly from the students, were thoroughly analyzed to develop a neural classifier employing convolutional neural networks. The results obtained revealed remarkable accuracy, surpassing 98%. This implementation has provided significant advances in performance and reliability in correcting tests, strengthening the effectiveness of the software.
