AB  - In this paper we propose a multifractal traffic model that is based on a multiplicative cascade presenting specific multiplier distributions in each cascade stage. In the proposed model, the multipliers are obtained through the estimate of their probability densities found in real network traffic by using Kernel and Acceptance/Rejection methods. Statistical analysis and queueing behavior study were carried out for the model validation. Furthermore, we verify the model performance in capturing the traffic trace characteristics in comparison to other multifractal models.
