TI  - Formal Semantics for Java-like Languages and Research Opportunities
FAU - Samuel da Silva Feitosa
FAU - Rodrigo Ribeiro
FAU - André Rauber Du Bois
DP  - 2018
AID - 10.22456/2175-2745.80912 [doi]
AB  - The objective of this paper is twofold: first, we discuss the state of art on Java-like semantics, focusing on those that provide formal specification using operational semantics (big-step or small-step), studying in detail the most cited projects and presenting some derivative works that extend the originals aggregating useful features. Also, we filter our research for those that provide some insights in type-safety proofs. Furthermore, we provide a comparison between the most used projects in order to show which functionalities are covered in such projects. Second, our effort is focused towards the research opportunities in this area, showing some important works that can be applied to the previously presented projects to study features of object-oriented languages, and pointing for some possibilities to explore in future researches.
